WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.281
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.581 --> 00:00:09.037
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.337 --> 00:00:15.785
Unit two: Third Conditional. Today you will reflect on the unreal past and its consequences.

4
00:00:16.085 --> 00:00:18.714
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:22.876
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.717 --> 00:00:24.729
If I had.

7
00:00:25.717 --> 00:00:28.680
If I had means the start of an unreal past condition.

8
00:00:29.283 --> 00:00:31.445
If I had known, I would have helped.

9
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.342
Your turn. Say: If I had.

10
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.143
If I had.

11
00:00:38.883 --> 00:00:39.826
Would have.

12
00:00:40.817 --> 00:00:43.397
Would have means the result in the third conditional.

13
00:00:43.983 --> 00:00:45.101
I would have gone.

14
00:00:45.717 --> 00:00:47.835
Your turn. Say: Would have.

15
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:51.678
Would have.

16
00:00:52.417 --> 00:00:53.789
Past hypothetical.

17
00:00:54.783 --> 00:00:58.350
Past hypothetical means an imagined situation in the past.

18
00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:00.984
It is a past hypothetical.

19
00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:04.665
Your turn. Say: Past hypothetical.

20
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.896
Past hypothetical.

21
00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:10.465
Regret.

22
00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:14.506
Regret means sadness about something done or not done.

23
00:01:15.117 --> 00:01:16.327
I feel regret.

24
00:01:16.917 --> 00:01:19.488
Your turn. Say: Regret.

25
00:01:22.333 --> 00:01:23.230
Regret.

26
00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.333
Unreal past.

27
00:01:26.317 --> 00:01:29.640
Unreal past means a past situation that did not happen.

28
00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:32.493
The unreal past cannot change.

29
00:01:33.083 --> 00:01:35.933
Your turn. Say: Unreal past.

30
00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:40.290
Unreal past.

31
00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:42.365
Missed opportunity.

32
00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:46.197
Missed opportunity means a chance that was not taken.

33
00:01:46.783 --> 00:01:48.527
It was a missed opportunity.

34
00:01:49.117 --> 00:01:52.431
Your turn. Say: Missed opportunity.

35
00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.581
Missed opportunity.

36
00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.562
Consequence.

37
00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.886
Consequence means a result of an action.

38
00:02:02.483 --> 00:02:04.332
The consequence was serious.

39
00:02:04.917 --> 00:02:07.476
Your turn. Say: Consequence.

40
00:02:10.333 --> 00:02:11.416
Consequence.

41
00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:13.163
Imagine.

42
00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:16.289
Imagine means to picture in the mind.

43
00:02:16.883 --> 00:02:18.686
Imagine you had left earlier.

44
00:02:19.283 --> 00:02:21.494
Your turn. Say: Imagine.

45
00:02:24.333 --> 00:02:25.265
Imagine.

46
00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:29.717
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.943
Visal, tell me about a missed opportunity.

48
00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:46.060
If I had applied for the scholarship, I might have studied abroad. The third conditional describes an unreal past: if + past perfect, would have + past participle.

49
00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:48.569
What does it express?

50
00:02:49.683 --> 00:02:58.301
Regret, criticism or relief about the past: If she hadn't taken the earlier train, she would have missed the accident. 

51
00:02:59.417 --> 00:03:00.766
Are there variations?

52
00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:11.468
We can use could have or might have for weaker results, and the inverted form in formal writing: Had I known, I would have called. We never use would have after if.

53
00:03:12.633 --> 00:03:14.470
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:15.317 --> 00:03:21.473
Grammar focus: Third conditional: If plus past perfect, would have plus past participle.

55
00:03:21.773 --> 00:03:23.041
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:26.539
If I had applied, I might have studied abroad.

57
00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:30.936
If she hadn't taken that train, she would have missed the accident.

58
00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:34.105
Had I known, I would have called you.

59
00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:42.618
If + past perfect, would / could / might have + past participle. Formal inversion: Had I known… Never use would have after if.

60
00:03:43.383 --> 00:03:46.941
Be careful! Don't say: If I would have known, I'd help.

61
00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:51.515
Say: If I had known, I would have helped.

62
00:03:51.815 --> 00:03:53.814
Use the past perfect after if.

63
00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.113
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.296
The Road Not Taken.

65
00:03:59.596 --> 00:04:03.070
If I had applied for the scholarship, I might have studied abroad.

66
00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:07.065
I missed that opportunity because I was afraid of failing.

67
00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:11.285
If I had taken the risk, my life would have been very different.

68
00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:15.135
Regret is an unavoidable consequence of living.

69
00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:19.898
Imagine how many chances we would have taken if we had known the outcome.

70
00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:25.002
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:28.291
If I blank harder, I would have passed.

72
00:04:28.591 --> 00:04:32.488
A, studied. B, had studied. C, would study.

73
00:04:36.033 --> 00:04:38.126
The answer is B: had studied.

74
00:04:39.283 --> 00:04:42.003
If she had left earlier, she blank the train.

75
00:04:42.303 --> 00:04:45.956
A, would have caught. B, will catch. C, caught.

76
00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.987
The answer is A: would have caught.

77
00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:55.266
'Had I known' is equivalent to blank.

78
00:04:55.566 --> 00:04:59.892
A, If I had known. B, If I knew. C, If I know.

79
00:05:03.433 --> 00:05:05.595
The answer is A: If I had known.

80
00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:07.937
Which is correct?

81
00:05:08.237 --> 00:05:15.420
A, If I would have known, I'd have helped.. B, If I had known, I'd have helped.. C, If I knew, I'd have helped..

82
00:05:18.967 --> 00:05:21.756
The answer is B: If I had known, I'd have helped..

83
00:05:22.917 --> 00:05:25.764
According to the reading, why did the writer miss the chance?

84
00:05:26.064 --> 00:05:30.530
A, fear of failing. B, lack of money. C, bad weather.

85
00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:36.484
The answer is A: fear of failing.

86
00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:41.165
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:42.017 --> 00:05:45.665
Describe one thing you would have done differently, using the third conditional.

88
00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:55.974
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:56.274 --> 00:06:08.472
If I had accepted the invitation to study abroad, I would have learned a new language and met many people. I did not go because I was nervous. I use the third conditional to express regret about the past.

90
00:06:08.772 --> 00:06:10.586
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:11.483 --> 00:06:19.244
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and third conditional: if plus past perfect, would have plus past participle.

92
00:06:19.544 --> 00:06:23.473
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

93
00:06:23.773 --> 00:06:26.182
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

94
00:06:26.482 --> 00:06:30.980
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

